# Telemetry provider config — NEVER commit.
#
# Since v1.5 Catalyst DOES link Firebase Analytics (opt-in, off by default). This file is its
# configuration: not a cryptographic secret — a copy ships inside every client binary — but it
# identifies the project and its quotas, and on a PUBLIC repo a single `git add -A` would publish
# it permanently, which git history does not let you quietly walk back.
#
# Its absence is the SUPPORTED state, not a broken one: `Telemetry.start()` resolves it by path and
# returns quietly when it isn't there, so a build from this repo compiles, launches, and sends
# nothing. Never "fix" a missing plist by committing one. The real file is CODEOWNERS-held and
# distributed out of band. See Telemetry/README.md.
Telemetry/GoogleService-Info.plist